    "body": "## Summary\n- make the Stripe Connect safe-retry deadline monotonic by anchoring it to the immutable payout request timestamp instead of `processingStartedAt`\n- prevent repeated stale-processing retries from continuously extending the effective provider idempotency window\n- add focused regression coverage for an old payout whose processing timestamp was refreshed shortly before recovery\n\n## Safety rationale\n`processingStartedAt` is cleared by `scheduleRetry()` and set again by `startProcessing()`. Using it as the 23h Stripe safety clock meant each retry could move the deadline forward. The request timestamp is immutable, making this conservative but fail-closed: an old queued payout may be quarantined earlier than strictly necessary, but automatic retry can no longer outlive the configured safety window.\n\n## Validation\n- focused JUnit regression test added\n- full GitHub Actions required before merge\n",
